# Per-project / instantiated files -- never tracked in the harness repo.
# Recipients generate these locally (/bootstrap, /on-board); pulls stay clean.
# Patterns are root-anchored so portable content (e.g. harness/templates/
# preferences_template.md) is never caught.
/settings.json
/settings.local.json
/preferences.md
/projects/

# Session markers written at runtime by the closing sequence, the orchestrator
# and the commands they dispatch. Every one is keyed to a live session_id and is
# meaningless to anyone else, so none is ever committed. The glob covers the
# `<thing>_session.json` naming every marker follows, so a marker added later is
# ignored without editing this file; phase_closing.json predates that convention
# and is listed on its own.
/phase_closing.json
/*_session.json

# Transient state
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
